Origin desktop — YOUR implementation goes here
=============================================
This directory is intentionally almost empty. It holds the contract;
you write the desktop.

Contract with the rest of the distro:
  1. Whatever you build must be installable as a Debian package
     (a second package next to origin-desktop, e.g. origin-shell).
  2. Its name goes into packages/origin-desktop/debian/control Depends:.
  3. Default user config ships via debian-live/config/includes.chroot/etc/skel/
     (shell.toml is already there as the example).
  4. Keybinds live in ONE file with the schema in keybinds.example.toml,
     so key handling stays uniform no matter which desktop you write.

Suggested order: keybind schema first (it's the interface), then the
smallest desktop that honors it, then package it.
